      "thinking": "Let me analyze this fragment of the OIML certificate.\n\nDocument-level:\n- number: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\" with \"Rev. 3\" — certificate number. The number includes \"Rev. 3\". I'll put number as \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\" and revision history exists. The schema doesn't have a \"revision\" at certificate level except revision_history. Hmm, the certificate number as given is \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02 Rev. 3\". I'll keep number: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\" and note Rev 3 in revision_history. Actually maybe include the full number as printed: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02 Rev. 3\"? The rule: don't fabricate. The certificate number is \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\", revision 3. I'll use \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\" as number. Or include \"Rev. 3\"? The revision history captures revision 3. I'll use number without revision.\n- scheme: \"A\" (issued under Scheme A)\n- project_number: not present. Maybe \"23.02\" is a project number? Not clear; skip.\n- page_total: 13 (\"Page 1 of 13 pages\")\n- member_state: \"SLOVAKIA\" / \"Slovakia\"\n- date_issued: 28 January 2025 (\"Date: 28st January 2025\")\n- oiml_issuer_id: not present explicitly? Not given. Omit.\n\nIssuing authority:\n- name: \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\"\n- address_lines: [\"Geologická 9966/1,\", \"821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice, Slovakia\", \"Product Certification Body\", \"Hviezdoslavova 31\", \"974 01 Banská Bystrica, Slovakia\"]\n- person_responsible: \"Ing. Dušan Šmigura, PhD.\" (Director of PCB)\n- person_title: \"Director of PCB\"\n- phone/email/website: not present.\n- oiml_issuer_id: not present.\n\nApplicants:\n- name: \"UAB „Axioma Metering“\"\n- address_lines: [\"Veterinaru str. 52, Biruliskes,\", \"LT-54469 Kaunas region,\", \"Lithuania\"]\n\nManufacturers: same.\n\nCertified type:\n- category: \"Water meter\"\n- type_designations: [\"Qalcosonic W1\", \"QALCOSONIC W1\"] — use \"Qalcosonic W1\" (also QALCOSONIC W1). I'll list [\"Qalcosonic W1\", \"QALCOSONIC W1\"]? Maybe just one: \"Qalcosonic W1\". The doc mentions both cases. I'll include both? Better to dedupe case-insensitively: [\"Qalcosonic W1\"]. I'll just use \"Qalcosonic W1\".\n- module_designation: \"Ultrasonic water meters with electronic indication device\" — that's the module designation field. Actually it says \"Designation of the module (if applicable): Ultrasonic water meters with electronic indication device\". Hmm, the module designation per R49... In water meter certs, the module is the combination. I'll put that string.\n- description: free-text description. I could include the summary from section 1: \"The ultrasonic water meter type QALCOSONIC W1 is designed to measure, memorise and display the volume of water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions...\" I'll include a condensed description.\n\nModel family: The cert covers DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32, DN40, and designs A and B (B only for DN15 and DN20). Models: DN15 A, DN15 B, DN20 A, DN20 B, DN25, DN32, DN40? The text says \"produced in A design (for all DNs) and design B (for DN15 and DN20 only)\". So models could be listed as DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32, DN40 with attribute design. I'll create model_family with models per DN, and maybe config-level for design.\n\nModels: \n- {\"model_id\": \"DN15\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\", \"B\"]}} — hmm, but schema says attributes{} — free-form. Could do {\"design_a\": true, \"design_b\": true}? Simpler: models for each DN, and config_level for design A vs B.\n\nI'll do:\nmodel_family: {family_name: \"Qalcosonic W1\", models: [{model_id: \"DN15\"}, {model_id: \"DN20\"}, {model_id: \"DN25\"}, {model_id: \"DN32\"}, {model_id: \"DN40\"}]}\n\nConfig level: axis \"design\", values: [{condition: \"design A\", ...}, {condition: \"design B (DN15 and DN20 only)\", ...}]? Hmm. config_level entries: attribute, axis, values: {condition, value}. Maybe attribute \"availability\", axis \"design\", values [{condition: \"A\", value: \"all DNs\"}, {condition: \"B\", value: \"DN15 and DN20 only\"}]. That's reasonable.\n\nCharacteristics type_level: The fragment doesn't have numeric characteristics tables (those are probably in later parts). Some things: display indication range 999999.999 m³, battery life 16 years. These are description details. Should I include them as type_level characteristics? Battery life 16 years could be: {battery_life: {value: 16, unit_symbol: \"years\"}}. Indication range 999999.999 m³: {display_indication_range: {value: 999999.999, unit_symbol: \"m³\"}}. These are legit. But rule 8: don't fabricate; these are present. I'll include battery life and display range.\n\nAccuracy classes: R49 accuracy class 2. Recommendation: id \"R49\", edition 2013, accuracy_classes: [2]. scheme — the recommendation scheme? The certificate scheme is A. The recommendation section has \"scheme\" field; probably the certificate scheme. I'll set scheme \"A\".\n\nTest reports:\n- {id: \"2025/ER006/SK1\", date: \"2025-01-28\", pages: 17, role: \"type_evaluation_report\"}\n- documentation files: \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_00\" dated 13 January 2023, 114 pages, role: documentation_file; \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_03\" dated 28 January 2025, 51 pages, documentation_file.\n\nRevision history:\n- {\"revision\": \"0\", \"date\": \"2023-01-13\", \"changes\": \"Certificate first issued\"}\n- {\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": \"2023-05-25\", \"changes\": \"Point 2.4 Software specification – supplemented specification for all DNs separately\"}\n- {\"revision\": \"2\", \"date\": \"2024-05-31\", \"changes\": \"Issued updated Evaluation Report No: 2022/ER010/SK1_ Rev. 1\"}\n- {\"revision\": \"3\", \"date\": \"2025-01-28\", \"changes\": \"Add design B (DN15 and DN20); Changed address of the issuing authority SLM on the EU-type examination certificate\"}\n\nDates: format? Use ISO \"2025-01-28\". Fine.\n\nFootnotes: none.\n\nComponents: Essential parts: flow sensor, calculator and indication device. Could list as components: flow sensor (role \"flow sensor\"), calculator and indication device. The fragment describes them. I could add components:\n- role: \"flow sensor\", description stuff. The components[] schema has role, type_designations[], alternatives, characteristics{}. No free description field... characteristics{} could hold attributes. Hmm. I could add components with role and characteristics for battery config? The battery configurations vary by DN — that's model-level. Maybe:\n  - component: role \"flow sensor\", characteristics {} \n  - component: role \"calculator and indication device\"\n\nBut type_designations aren't given. Maybe skip components or include minimal. I think include components with role and characteristics for relevant details:\n\n- {\"role\": \"flow_sensor\", \"characteristics\": {\"sound_paths\": ...}}? That might be over-engineering. The fragment: \"the inner plastic element with two mirrors (four mirrors for DN40)\" — sound paths vary by DN: model_level attribute \"number_of_mirrors\" / \"ultrasonic_transducers\": 2 (DN15-DN32), 4 (DN40). Could add model_level entries:\n  - attribute \"ultrasonic_transducer_count\": DN15: 2, DN20: 2, DN25: 2, DN32: 2, DN40: 4\n  - attribute \"mirror_count\": same.\n\nHmm, that's inferring from \"(four mirrors for DN40)\" — the text says two mirrors, four for DN40, and two transducers (four for DN40). That's legitimate extraction. I'll include in model_level? It's about components though. Could put in components characteristics as config/model. The components characteristics{} is free-form object. Let me do:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {\"role\": \"flow_sensor\", \"characteristics\": {\"sound_path_mirrors\": {\"default\": 2, \"DN40\": 4}, \"ultrasonic_transducers\": {\"default\": 2, \"DN40\": 4}}}\n]\n\nBut rule 2 says every characteristic value MUST be the structured object shape... that applies to characteristics values. To be safe, use structured objects:\n\n\"characteristics\": {\n  \"sound_path_mirrors\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": null},\n  ...\n}\n\nHmm but the DN40 variation. I could put model_level entries instead:\ncharacteristics.model_level:\n- {attribute: \"number_of_mirrors\", values: [{model: \"DN15\", value: 2}, {model: \"DN20\", value: 2}, {model: \"DN25\", value: 2}, {model: \"DN32\", value: 2}, {model: \"DN40\", value: 4}]}\n- same for ultrasonic transducers.\n\nWait — is \"two mirrors\" true for all DNs except DN40? Text: \"the inner plastic element with two mirrors (four mirrors for DN40)\". Yes. Transducers: \"two ultrasonic transducers (four for DN40)\". Yes.\n\nBattery configs vary by DN and design — messy text with apparent errors (\"for DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32 two internal batteries AA\"; then \"for DN15 and DN15 B design, DN20 and DN20 B design, DN25, DN32: two AA + one A23\"; \"For DN15 B design, DN20 B design one C + one A23\"; \"for DN40 one D\"; \"for DN40 one D + one A23\"). These are contradictory/overlapping; risky to structure. Maybe describe in matrix_tables? Rule: don't fabricate. I could record as a matrix_table \"battery_configuration\" with rows per DN/design, quoting text. That's messy. I'll perhaps skip detailed battery matrix and just mention battery life 16 years as type_level and battery types in components. Actually let me consider including a matrix_tables entry:\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"Battery configuration by nominal size and design\",\n  \"columns\": [\"nominal_size\", \"design\", \"battery_configuration\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"nominal_size\": \"DN15\", \"design\": \"A\", \"battery_configuration\": \"two internal batteries \\\"AA\\\" size + one \\\"A23\\\"\"},\n    ...\n  ]\n}\n\nBut the text is contradictory (first bullet says DN15–DN32 two AA; second says DN15/15B/20/20B/25/32 two AA + A23). Likely revision 3 added design B with C+A23 for B designs. The second bullet overrides for A designs with +A23? Actually bullet order: \n1. for DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32 two internal batteries \"AA\" size;\n2. for DN15 and DN15 B design, DN20 and DN20 B design, DN25, DN32: two internal batteries \"AA\" size + one \"A23\";\n3. For DN15 B design, DN20 B design one internal battery \"C\" size + one \"A23\";\n4. for DN40 one internal battery \"D\" size;\n5. for DN40 one internal battery \"D\" size + one \"A23\".\n\nThis is OCR of a list possibly with strikethrough revisions. Too risky. I'll record battery info qualitatively: type_level \"battery_life\": 16 years; and in description mention battery configurations. I'll put battery details in the certified_type description string? The description field is \"free-text description if present\". I can include a summarized description. I'll keep description focused on the type description from section 1 and key parts.\n\nLet me draft description: \"Ultrasonic water meter (compact, with electronic indication device) measuring volume of clean water for residential use by the bidirectional transit-time ultrasonic principle. Essential parts: flow sensor (brass body with plastic housing, inner element with two mirrors — four for DN40 — and two ultrasonic transducers — four for DN40) and calculator with indication device (LCD with 9-digit upper line for volume, 5-digit lower line for flow rate, non-replaceable lithium batteries with 16-year life). Non-essential parts: antenna and optional non-return valve. Produced in design A (all DN) and design B (DN15 and DN20 only); difference is external appearance only.\"\n\nMaybe too long but acceptable. Actually maybe I shouldn't editorialize; but a condensed description is fine.\n\nType-level characteristics:\n- battery_life: {value: 16, unit_symbol: \"years\"}\n- display_volume_indication_range: {value: 999999.999, unit_symbol: \"m³\"}\n- display_flow_rate_digits: 5? Maybe skip.\n\nmodel_level:\n- number_of_sound_path_mirrors: DN15 2, DN20 2, DN25 2, DN32 2, DN40 4\n- number_of_ultrasonic_transducers: same pattern\n\nconfig_level:\n- attribute: \"availability_of_design\", axis: \"design\"? Hmm. Actually config_level values: {condition, value, unit_symbol}. I'll do:\n{\n  \"attribute\": \"design_availability\",\n  \"axis\": \"design\",\n  \"values\": [\n    {\"condition\": \"design A\", \"value\": \"all nominal sizes (DN15–DN40)\"},\n    {\"condition\": \"design B\", \"value\": \"DN15 and DN20 only\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nHmm value as string OK per rule 2 (string allowed).\n\nAlso installation positions: \"can be installed to operate in horizontal and vertical positions\" — type_level: {installation_positions: {value: \"horizontal and vertical\"}}? Could include. And \"not designed to measure the reverse flow\" — measurement of reverse flow: false. Might include as type_level: {\"reverse_flow_measurement\": {\"value\": false}}? Hmm, maybe. I'll include installation_positions as string \"horizontal and vertical\". Eh, could be nice. I'll include.\n\nCertificate level fields: date_issued \"2025-01-28\". member_state \"Slovakia\".\n\nproject_number: There's \"23.02\" in the certificate number possibly. Also \"FK-P05-85\" is form number, \"V04/24-12-02\" form version. Skip.\n\npage_total: 13.\n\nRecommendation: {id: \"R49\", edition: 2013, accuracy_classes: [2], scheme: \"A\"}. Actually \"scheme\" in recommendation — certificate scheme A. Include.\n\nCertificate number: \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\". Include \"Rev. 3\"? revision_history covers. I'll use number \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\".\n\nTest report date: \"28st January 2025\" (typo in original, 28th) → 2025-01-28.\n\nDocumentation file names: 'AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_00\"' — there's a stray quote; actual likely `AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_00`. Use \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_00\" and \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_03\".\n\nAlso revision 2 mentions Evaluation Report 2022/ER010/SK1 Rev. 1 — that's history, maybe add to revision changes only.\n\nIssuing authority address: two addresses (Bratislava registered + PCB in Banská Bystrica). Include both in address_lines with \"Product Certification Body\" line.\n\nperson_responsible: \"Ing. Dušan Šmigura, PhD.\" person_title: \"Director of PCB\". Signature at bottom is \"Dušan Šmigura\".\n\nNow the module_designation: \"Ultrasonic water meters with electronic indication device\". Schema says module_designation is \"Analog load cell\" | \"Not applicable\" | null examples, but for water meter it's this string. Fine.\n\nCategory: \"Water meter\".\n\nmodel_family.family_name: \"Qalcosonic W1\".\n\nmodels: DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32, DN40. Include attributes: design B available for DN15/DN20: attributes: {\"design_b_available\": true/false}? I could add: DN15: {\"designs\": [\"A\",\"B\"]}, DN20: [\"A\",\"B\"], DN25/32/40: [\"A\"]. That's derived but accurate. I'll include.\n\nmatrix_tables: skip (battery config too messy)? Or include battery table with rows and note. I think including it with careful wording is valuable but risks fabrication. The instruction says preserve multi-dim tables that don't fit elsewhere. The battery list is a bullet list, not table. I'll skip matrix_tables, but I can include battery configuration in description.\n\nActually, maybe I include the battery config as model/config-level? The contradiction: bullet 1 vs bullet 2 for DN15-DN32. It looks like bullet 1 was the original and bullet 2 updated (or OCR merged two versions). Rule 8: don't fabricate. Safer to omit structured battery config and mention in description briefly? Even description summarizing contradictory list is risky. I'll mention \"non-replaceable lithium batteries (AA/A23/C/D sizes depending on DN and design), life 16 years\". That's a fair summary.\n\nFootnotes: none present.\n\nOutput JSON only.\n\nLet me also double check \"accuracy class 2\" — \"For accuracy class (if applicable): 2\". R49 has accuracy classes 1 and 2. So accuracy_classes: [2].\n\ndate_issued: The signature date 28 January 2025. Also revision 3 date same. Good.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-23.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 13,\n    \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2025-01-28\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\n      \"Geologická 9966/1,\",\n      \"821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice, Slovakia\",\n      \"Product Certification Body\",\n      \"Hviezdoslavova 31\",\n      \"974 01 Banská Bystrica, Slovakia\"\n    ],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Ing. Dušan Šmigura, PhD.\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Director of PCB\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"UAB „Axioma Metering“\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Veterinaru str. 52, Biruliskes,\", \"LT-54469 Kaunas region,\", \"Lithuania\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    { same }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"Qalcosonic W1\"],\n    \"module_designation\": \"Ultrasonic water meters with electronic indication device\",\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"Qalcosonic W1\",\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN15\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\", \"B\"]}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN20\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\", \"B\"]}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN25\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\"]}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN32\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\"]}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"DN40\", \"attributes\": {\"designs\": [\"A\"]}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"type_level\": {\n      \"battery_life\": {\"value\": 16, \"unit_symbol\": \"years\", \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"volume_indication_range\": {\"value\": 999999.999, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\", \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"installation_positions\": {\"value\": \"horizontal and vertical\", \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}\n    },\n    \"model_level\": [\n      {\"attribute\": \"number_of_sound_path_mirrors\", \"values\": [{\"model\": \"DN15\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"DN20\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"DN25\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"DN32\", \"value\": 2}, {\"model\": \"DN40\", \"value\": 4}]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"number_of_ultrasonic_transducers\", \"values\": [same pattern]}\n    ],\n    \"config_level\": [\n      {\n        \"attribute\": \"design_availability\",\n        \"axis\": \"design\",\n        \"values\": [\n          {\"condition\": \"design A\", \"value\": \"all nominal sizes DN15–DN40\"},\n          {\"condition\": \"design B\", \"value\": \"DN15 and DN20 only\"}\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [2]},\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\"id\": \"2025/ER006/SK1\", \"date\": \"2025-01-28\", \"pages\": 17, \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_00\", \"date\": \"2023-01-13\", \"pages\": 114, \"role\": \"documentation_file\"},\n    {\"id\": \"AXIOMA_Qalcosonic W1_03\", \"date\": \"2025-01-28\", \"pages\": 51, \"role\": \"documentation_file\"}\n  ],\n  \"revision_history\": [...]\n}\n\nNote: rule 2's structured shape includes unit_symbol and footnote_markers — footnote_markers optional. unit_id optional? The shape includes unit_id; I'll include unit_id: null where needed or omit. Rule 8 says omit fields not present. unit_id: null fine.\n\nThe structured shape: should each value include \"unit_id\"? The example shows unit_symbol and unit_id. To be consistent, include unit_id: null. I'll include.\n\nFor model_level values, shape {model, value, footnote_markers[]} — unit at attribute level. Good.\n\nAlso flow-rate display line 5 digits — maybe add type_level \"flow_rate_display_digits\": 5? Minor. And volume display 9 digits with 3 decimals. I'll add \"volume_display_digits\": 9? Eh, maybe keep it lean. I'll include the indication range only.\n\nDesign difference: \"lies solely in the external appearance. The measurement section is identical.\" Could add config_level note. Included in description.\n\nDescription text — compose:\n\n\"Compact ultrasonic water meter with electronic indication device for measuring, memorising and displaying the volume of clean water in residential use (non-resettable measurements between two constant partners). Measurement based on the ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time principle. Essential parts: flow sensor (cylindrical brass body with plastic calculator housing, inner plastic element with two mirrors — four for DN40 — and two ultrasonic transducers — four for DN40) and calculator with directly mounted indication device (LCD: upper line 9 digits, indication range 999999.999 m³; lower line 5 digits for flow rate in m³/h), powered by non-replaceable lithium batteries (AA/A23/C/D sizes depending on DN and design) with 16-year life. Non-essential parts: antenna, optional non-return valve. Can be installed in horizontal and vertical positions; not designed to measure reverse flow. Produced in design A (all DNs) and design B (DN15 and DN20 only); the difference is solely the external appearance, the measurement section is identical.\"\n\nOK.\n\nAlso should I mention type name variant \"QALCOSONIC W1\"? type_designations: [\"Qalcosonic W1\", \"QALCOSONIC W1\"]? Same instrument, different casing. I'll just use \"Qalcosonic W1\".\n\ncomponent entries? I described parts within description. Components with role: \"flow_sensor\", \"calculator_and_indication_device\" — could add:\n\n\"components\": [\n  {\"role\": \"flow_sensor\", \"characteristics\": {}},\n  {\"role\": \"calculator_and_indication_device\", \"characteristics\": {}}\n]\n\nEmpty characteristics feel useless. Maybe include with characteristics: transducers count etc. But I already put transducer counts in model_level. I'll skip components[] since type designations for components aren't named. Actually schema: include ONLY if cert names sub-assemblies. The cert names \"flow sensor\", \"calculator and indication device\" as essential parts. It's borderline. I'll include them with brief characteristics (non-replaceable lithium batteries for calculator). Let me include:\n\ncomponents: [\n  {\n    \"role\": \"flow_sensor\",\n    \"characteristics\": {\n      \"sound_path_mirrors\": ... — no, model-varying, already in model_level.\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nI'll skip components to avoid duplication/noise. Hmm, but the instructions encourage components for sub-assemblies. The measurement section names: flow sensor, calculator and indication device. I'll include minimal entries without characteristics — that's allowed? characteristics{} free-form; could include note. I'll include them with short characteristics like {\"description\": \"...\"}? characteristics{} is object of attributes; description inside might violate structure rule 2 (every characteristic value must be structured). I'll skip components. The description covers it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: rule 2 says every characteristic value MUST be object with value/unit_symbol/unit_id/footnote_markers. So free-form strings inside characteristics are not allowed. Skip components.\n\nConfig-level design availability: value strings \"all nominal sizes (DN15, DN20, DN25, DN32, DN40)\" and \"DN15 and DN20 only\". Good.\n\nAlso add type_level \"measurement_principle\"? Not needed.\n\nCheck certificate project_number: absent. oiml_issuer_id: absent.\n\nDates: revision 1: 25 May 2023 → 2023-05-25. Revision 2: 31 May 2024 → 2024-05-31.\n\nRevision 3 changes: \"Add design B (DN15 and DN20); Changed address of the issuing authority SLM on the EU-type examination certificate\". Keep with semicolon.\n\nOutput final JSON.",
